  "limitations": [
    "Win11 default differential remains failed (102 native vs 103 reference). One reference PID exceeds u32 in a damaged process chain. Native rejects it; no reference filtering or false passing status.",
    "Both-sided absent optional audit/PEB paths are counted as matched_absent, never recovered data. One-sided absence still fails. All native real-image results are partial.",
    "True is only a Unicode descriptor length mismatch (including spare MaximumLength capacity and surrogate code-point/unit differences), not proof of malicious masquerading. False does not prove clean inputs when descriptors are absent or unreadable.",
    "Native EPROCESS.Peb is used for WOW64 processes as in the reference; no separate WOW64 PEB view is substituted.",
    "PID list supports up to 4096 items, unions --pid/--pids and deduplicates. Real cases cover single PID, null-PEB kernel PID and union selection.",
    "Only x86/x64 are supported. Additional Windows builds, confirmed masquerading attacks and broader damaged-input cases still require validation.",
    "Original user image c8f6a7f79a5a83d238b1ff16c2a51277d56b6e16580f7db5706b38bcfd5a5c66 remains unavailable and untested."
  ]
